// ── D1 round 14: THE FOURTH CHANNEL ───────────────────────────────────────
// `collect_ref_sources_paths` (§B6) is the borrow checker's FOURTH provenance
// walker. It is not a peer of the three the coverage table had columns for
// (`ref_source_places`, `ref_sources_of`, the summarizer's `taint_of`): it
// answers a different question for a DIFFERENT VERDICT — `ref_borrow_sources_`
// is read by `pop_scope` to raise E0597 ("does not live long enough"). So an
// omission here never moved the `c.bump()` verdict that every round from 1 to
// 13 used as its witness, and twelve rounds of shapes could not see it.
//
// Q6 — THE GATE, not the shape. `is_borrow_carrying_type` names Enum/Struct/
// ZonedStruct, so it answers NO for a bare `&i64` and therefore NO for
// `Option<&i64>`: a call returning an OPTION OF A REFERENCE tied its result to
// nothing. Widened to `type_may_carry_borrow`, round 9/11's predicate for
// exactly this question, which round 13 / P1 already moved TupleIndex and
// IndexRead onto. Measured WITHOUT `?`, so this is not the Try arm's problem.
// TWIN: bc_d1r14_q4_call_twin (the same call returning `&i64` directly).
package bc_d1r14_q6_optcall;
// Is the Call gate the blocker? Same call, NO `?` — bind the Option itself.
use logos.lang.option;
fn pick(v: &i64) -> Option<&i64> { return Option::Some(v); }
fn main() -> i32 {
    let mut o: Option<&i64>;
    { let x: i64 = 7i64; o = pick(&x); }
    match o { Option::Some(r) => { return *r as i32; } Option::None => { return 0i32; } }
}
